             are all scapy fictions, crafted at L2 with the DUT's SVI MAC as the
             next hop, so the kernel's own addresses and routes are bypassed
             entirely. NO host networking was changed at any point.
  unused   : the partner switches on consoles u3 and u5 were NEVER touched by this
             case -- not read, not written. The PDU was not used; the reboot in
             STEP 5 is a CLI `reload`.
  STP      : read immediately before every counted leg, so that no zero can be an
             L2 effect:
               port1.0.10  0000:e01aead47043  8392  Designated  Forwarding
               port1.0.48  0000:e01aead47043  83b8  Designated  Forwarding
  tools    : tools/arpleg.py (every counted leg: it starts tcpdump on each NIC
             named, sends a known count of crafted frames from one of them, stops,
             and prints a grouped count with the Ethernet src/dst of every flow;
             `--answer IP=MAC --answer-iface <nic>` runs a background ARP responder
