        x4  ARP-REQ who-has 172.16.10.1 tell 172.16.10.5   -> 0 replies  (was 4)

  4b. FORWARDING. --tag L5b-route-removed, eth4 -> watch eth3:
      cap on eth3: x5  ICMP 192.168.48.9 -> 192.168.10.9 only, plus the DUT's ARP for it
      cap on eth4: x2  ICMP t3/c0 192.168.48.1 -> 192.168.48.9
      172.16.10.5  : 5 sent, 0 arrived   (was 5)
      192.168.10.9 : 5 sent, 5 arrived -- instrument alive, so the zero is a measurement

  => STEP 4 PASS: the no-form takes the secondary out of the DATAPLANE as well as
     out of running-config, on both discriminators at once and both reversing
     cleanly -- ARP from 4 of 4 back to 0 of 4 for the very sender that had been
     answered, and forwarding from 5 of 5 back to 0 of 5 -- with the connected
     route gone and the instrument control still carrying 5 of 5 in the same leg.

